      <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-lg border border-border-subtle bg-bg-surface">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">Summary</h2>
        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-3">
          <strong>Light mode</strong> already passes AAA with the current accent — no change needed.
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-3">
          <strong>Dark mode</strong> is the only gap for AAA. The trade-off is that achieving 7:1 requires
          lightening the accent, which makes it more pastel. <strong>Option A
          (<code class="font-mono text-sm">#9F92D8</code>)</strong> is the closest to the current feel —
          a subtle lightening that just crosses the AAA threshold at 7.09:1.
          <strong>Option B (<code class="font-mono text-sm">#A89CDF</code>)</strong> provides more margin
          at 7.94:1 but is noticeably lighter.
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
          The current dark mode accent (5.70:1) comfortably passes AA, which is the standard expectation.
          AAA is aspirational — whether the visual trade-off of a lighter accent is worth the gain
          is a design judgement.
        </p>
